@page
@model Howtobid
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "How to Bid";
}


<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="divider">How to Bid for Acquired Properties</div>
        <h3>A Simple, Transparent Guide to Purchasing Bank Assets</h3>
        <p style="max-width:640px;">Acquiring real estate through Rural Bank of Norala is a straightforward and secure process. Whether you are bidding on agricultural land, a residential lot, or a commercial space, our bidding framework ensures fairness, clear documentation, and total transparency.</p>
        <p style="max-width:640px;">All bank-acquired properties (Real and Other Properties Acquired - ROPA) are sold on an "As-Is, Where-Is" basis through sealed competitive bidding or direct negotiation.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="divider">The Bidding Process</div>
        <h3>Step-by-Step</h3>

        <div class="grid grid-3" style="margin-top:30px;">
            <div class="card">
                <h3>1. Select &amp; Inspect the Property</h3>
                <p style="font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--color-soil); font-weight:600;">Due Diligence</p>
                <p>Review our Available Properties inventory and conduct an actual site visit. Inspect the property's physical condition, boundaries, accessibility, and neighborhood.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <h3>2. Prepare Your Bid Documents</h3>
                <p style="font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--color-soil); font-weight:600;">Document Preparation</p>
                <p>Obtain an official Bid Form / Letter of Intent from the Rural Bank of Norala main office. Fill out your details, your proposed purchase price, and your preferred payment mode (Cash or Bank Financing).</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <h3>3. Submit Your Sealed Bid</h3>
                <p style="font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--color-soil); font-weight:600;">Main Office Submission</p>
                <p>Place your completed Bid Form and a refundable Bid Security / Deposit (typically 10% of your offer) in a sealed envelope. Submit it to our Asset Management Committee at our main office before the specified deadline.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-2" style="margin-top:20px;">
            <div class="card">
                <h3>4. Bid Opening &amp; Notification</h3>
                <p style="font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--color-soil); font-weight:600;">Evaluation &amp; Approval</p>
                <p>The bank's Asset Management Committee reviews all sealed bids. The highest qualifying bid that meets or exceeds the bank's minimum floor price will be recommended for Board approval. You will be notified in writing of the results.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <h3>5. Payment &amp; Deed Signing</h3>
                <p style="font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--color-soil); font-weight:600;">Final Execution</p>
                <p>Upon approval, pay the balance according to your agreed terms (Cash or Down Payment for Bank Financing) and sign the Deed of Absolute Sale or Contract to Sell.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="divider">Modes of Payment</div>
        <h3>Flexible Options Depending on Your Financial Preferences</h3>

        <table class="data-table" style="margin-top:30px;">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Payment Mode</th>
                    <th>Details &amp; Benefits</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Cash / Spot Payment</strong></td>
                    <td>Pay the full approved purchase price within 30 days of approval. Special cash discounts may apply.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>In-House Bank Financing</strong></td>
                    <td>Pay a required down payment (usually 20% to 30%) and finance the remaining balance over 1 to 5 years via fixed monthly installments.</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="divider">Requirements</div>
        <h3>Requirements for Bidders</h3>
        <p style="max-width:640px;">When submitting your bid, please include copies of the following documents:</p>

        <div class="grid grid-2" style="margin-top:30px;">
            <div class="card">
                <h3>For Individual Bidders</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Fully accomplished Bid Form</li>
                    <li>Copy of 2 valid Government-Issued IDs (e.g., PhilID, Driver's License, Passport, UMID)</li>
                    <li>Proof of Income / Financial Capacity (e.g., Bank Statements, ITR, Farm/Business Records)</li>
                    <li>Bid Deposit / Security check or cash voucher</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <h3>For Corporations or Cooperatives</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>SEC / CDA Registration Documents &amp; Articles of Incorporation</li>
                    <li>Board Resolution / Secretary's Certificate authorizing the representative to bid</li>
                    <li>Valid IDs of the authorized signatory</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="divider">Important Bidding Rules &amp; Disclaimers</div>
        <h3>Please Read Carefully Before Bidding</h3>

        <div class="grid grid-3" style="margin-top:30px;">
            <div class="card">
                <h3>"As-Is, Where-Is" Basis</h3>
                <p>All properties are sold in their current physical and legal condition. Bidders are responsible for verifying titles, tax declarations, property boundaries, and occupant status prior to submitting a bid.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <h3>Right to Reject</h3>
                <p>Rural Bank of Norala reserves the right to reject any or all bids, waive formal defects, or accept the bid deemed most advantageous to the bank.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
                <h3>Refund of Bid Security</h3>
                <p>Unsuccessful bidders will have their bid security/deposit returned in full without interest following the evaluation period.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>